## 3. `src/api/` — HTTP surface

Express, mounted alongside the existing `METRICS_PORT` server or on its own
`API_PORT`. Versioned under `/api/v1`.

| Method | Path | Behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/v1/tokens/:mint/report` | Latest report + evidence + errors + forensics linkage → `RiskView`. `404` if never analysed. |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/tokens/:mint/forensics` | Phase 5 run detail: analyzers, wallet clusters, eligibility assessment. |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/tokens/:mint/scan` | Idempotent enqueue. Returns `{ jobKey, status }`. Re-request with a live job returns the existing job. |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/jobs/:jobKey` | Job status polling. |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/health` | Liveness + DB reachability. |

Rules:

- `:mint` validated with `PublicKey` before any query. Reject early, 400.
- Reuse the Phase 4 `assetResolver` so a future EVM surface needs no reshaping.
- Rate limit per API key and per IP. Enqueue is the expensive path — cap it
  independently and far lower than reads.
- Auth: bearer key from `API_KEYS` (comma-separated) for `POST`; `GET` may be
  public if you intend a public good, but rate-limited regardless.
- Never return raw `rawPayload` blobs or internal error stack traces.

