## 4. `src/telegram/` — bot client

grammY. Long polling (no webhook, no public ingress, no TLS termination to
manage). Its own process: `npm run telegram`.

Do not add a second login of an existing token in a running process — see
ARCHITECTURE.md §13.8. One Telegram process, one token.

### 4.1 Commands

| Input | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| `/start` | What this bot does, what it cannot do, the "no safe verdict" caveat. |
| `/scan <mint>` | Fetch report. If absent → enqueue, reply with job status, edit the message in place when complete. |
| bare base58 string | Treated as `/scan`. This is the main path — people paste addresses. |
| `/status <mint>` | Current job/forensics status without enqueueing. |
| `/explain <signal>` | Static text explaining what bundled supply / wallet clustering / wash trading mean and how they're measured. |

### 4.2 Constraints

- Never accepts, stores, or requests a private key, seed phrase, or wallet
  connection. If a user sends something resembling one, discard it unlogged and
  warn them to rotate it immediately.
- Per-chat rate limit and a global enqueue budget.
- No inline "buy" buttons, no referral links to trading bots, no affiliate
  routing. The moment this bot monetises the click it stops being a defence.
- Talks to the API over HTTP, or imports `src/presentation/` + Prisma reads
  directly. It does not reimplement projection logic either way.

